# Project conventions and known drift

This file belongs to **this project** — `papa new` only seeds it, and nothing refreshes it automatically.
Keep it current: it is what tells an assistant (or a new teammate) how this repository is laid out and
where it has already diverged from current Papa.

## Layout

| Path | What goes there |
| --- | --- |
| `sites/{{.Module}}.go` | site + stage declaration (Key / BaseURL / Headers / Breaker / Stages). Self-registers via `init()` + `papa.RegisterSite`. |
| `fetcher/<site>/` | stage handlers and entry submission — one package per site once there is more than one |
| `models/` | business structs and GORM table models; `models.Models()` is the migration list |
| `monitor/` | back-office layers: `tables.go` / `controller/` / `view/` / `router.go` / `middleware.go` |
| `docs/` | a copy of the framework manuals (may lag the framework — see `references/doc-map.md`) |
| `.claude/skills/` | this skill. `papa new` writes it; `papa upgrade --write` refreshes `SKILL.md` + `references/{doc-map,implementation-patterns,review-checklist}.md` when they drift, but **never this file** (project-owned). |

## Conventions

- **Stage names are unique *within a site*** (`v3.4.0`+; the engine keys a stage by `site:stage`). Two sites
  may each declare `catalog`, so **no site prefix is needed** — define the constants once in the fetcher
  package and reuse them in `GetStage`, `Task.Stage`, tests and diagnostics. A duplicate *within one site*
  fails at startup and names the site.
- Stage parameters (worker count, queue size, delay, retry, `Entry`, downloader overrides) live in the
  `sites/` declaration — **not** in `config.yaml`.
- `main.go` stays generic: `monitor.Register(app)` plus `app.RegisterSites(papa.Sites()...)`. Adding a
  site is adding a file.
- The three governance queues (`error_queue` / `recover_queue` / `repeat_queue`) are **global**, configured
  in `config.yaml`.
- Business identity travels in `Task.Meta`; it is persisted with the row and restored by every requeue path.

## Known drift (add a line whenever you find one)

The framework moves; this project may still carry "that used to be right" code, comments or config.
Record it here — **where**, **what is correct now**, **when you found it**. The audit workflow in
`SKILL.md` consults this list first, so the more concrete it is, the less re-discovery is needed.

